.TH WIILAND-CONFIG 1 "August 2026" "wiiland" "WiiLand Manual"
.SH NAME
wiiland-config \- graphical WiiLand configuration and diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wiiland-config
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wiiland-config
opens the WiiLand Control Center, a native eframe/egui application.  It edits
Wii Remote profiles and device rules, invokes
.BR wiilandd (1)
for configuration and diagnostics, captures event traces and motion
calibration, and controls the per-user systemd service.
.PP
The initial window is 1180 by 780 pixels and cannot be resized below 760 by
600.  The application id is
.BR io.github.philosophimoonbeam.wiiland-config .
The native window backend is selected by eframe for the current session; the
Overview status reports Wayland when WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set, X11 when DISPLAY
is set otherwise, and unknown when neither is set.
.PP
The frontend does not create input devices or run a private daemon.  All
commands run asynchronously, with their standard output and standard error
shown in the Command output panel.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
On startup the frontend selects the user path
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is absolute.  Otherwise, when HOME is absolute, it uses
.B $HOME/.config/wiiland/wiilandd.conf .
If neither environment variable yields an absolute path, the daemon system
path
.B /etc/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
is used as the editable target.
.PP
The initial load runs
.B wiilandd --dump-config
without
.B --config
for the default user target, so the daemon's optional system file is layered
before its optional user file.  If a different path is entered, config-
sensitive commands receive
.B --config
with that path and use that file alone.  The entered path is also the save
target.  Device listing and axis-map commands do not receive a config path.
.PP
Configuration values use the daemon's canonical key=value tokens.  See
.BR wiilandd (1)
for all accepted keys, ranges, defaults, and layering rules.
.SH OVERVIEW TAB
The Overview tab provides editable Daemon executable and Configuration file
fields and reports the selected configuration scope and detected window
system.  Its controls are:
.TP
.B Reload from daemon
Run wiilandd --dump-config and replace the form with the resolved values.
.TP
.B Refresh service
Run
.BR "systemctl --user is-active wiilandd.service" .
.TP
.B Start , Stop , Restart
Run the corresponding
.BR "systemctl --user"
operation for
.BR wiilandd.service .
.TP
.B Check readiness
Run
.B "wiilandd --doctor"
\&.
.TP
.B Validate configuration
Run
.B "wiilandd --check-config"
\&.
.TP
.B Show effective config
Run
.B wiilandd --dump-config .
.TP
.B Find devices
Run
.BR "wiilandd --list --verbose" .
.TP
.B View input map
Run
.B wiilandd --axis-map .
.TP
.B View test checklist
Run
.B wiilandd --validation-checklist .
.SH CONFIGURATION TAB
The Configuration tab contains controls for every editable daemon setting:
.TP
.B Profiles and pointer feel
Default profile (gamepad, desktop, or both), D-pad pointer speed, IR gain,
IR jitter deadzone, IR smoothing, IR tracking (dual, centroid, or first), IR
aim mapping (relative or absolute), and optional IR screen calibration bounds.
.TP
.B Modern motion aiming
Output (off, right stick, or mouse), sensor (automatic, IR, MotionPlus, or
accelerometer), activation (always, B, Nunchuk Z, or Nunchuk C), sensitivity,
deadzone, smoothing, X/Y inversion, independent accelerometer and MotionPlus
calibration toggles and X/Y/Z fields, and calibration duration.
.TP
.B Desktop button bindings
Actions for Wii Remote A, B, +, -, Home, 1, and 2.  Each action is one of
disabled, left-click, right-click, enter, escape, overview, page-up, or
page-down.
.TP
.B Per-device profile rules
Add or remove up to 32 ordered rules.  Each rule matches a substring of either
the device path or device type and selects gamepad, desktop, or both.  Later
matching rules override earlier matches.
.PP
Numeric widgets constrain values to the daemon's accepted ranges.  Changes are
marked unsaved.  The controls below the scrollable settings are:
.TP
.B Reload from daemon
Discard edits and reload effective daemon configuration.
.TP
.B Validate and save
Validate the form with wiilandd --check-config against a same-directory
temporary file.  On success, atomically replace the selected target; on
failure, preserve the existing file.
.TP
.B Save and restart daemon
Available only for the default user target.  Save as above and then run
.B "systemctl --user restart wiilandd.service"
\&.  It is disabled for an
explicit target because the installed service does not load that target.
.SH VALIDATION TAB
The Validation tab accepts an optional device selector (a positive ordinal or
sysfs path), an event filter (all, keys, axes, ir, or motion-plus), and an
optional temporary profile (effective configuration, gamepad, desktop, or
both).
.TP
.B Start trace
Run wiilandd with
.BR --dry-run ,
.BR --trace-events ,
and
.B --verbose .  A selected device is passed through
.BR --device .
No virtual input is created.
.TP
.B Stop
Request termination of the active trace or calibration process.
.TP
.B Capture flat-surface calibration
Run
.BR --calibrate-aim
with the configured sample duration and optional device selector.  Successful
output is applied to the form and marked unsaved; save it to persist the
values.
.PP
Trace and calibration are mutually exclusive.  Suggested coverage shown in
the tab includes Wii Remote, MotionPlus, Nunchuk, Classic Controller, Wii U
Pro Controller, Guitar, Drums, Balance Board, SDL, Wine/Proton, and desktop
input on Wayland and X11.
.SH COMMAND OUTPUT
The fixed-width Command output panel displays commands, stdout, stderr, and
process errors.  Copy all copies the complete retained text to the clipboard;
Clear removes it.  The buffer retains at most 10,000 text blocks.  Completion
results that belong to an old form revision or target are discarded, and a
failed save preserves existing data.
.PP
Closing with unsaved changes opens an Unsaved configuration dialog.  Discard
changes closes the application; Keep editing returns to the form.
.SH PERMISSIONS
The frontend does not elevate privileges.  The selected configuration target
and its parent must be writable to save.  Service controls require a working
systemd user manager.  The daemon itself requires access to hid-wiimote input
nodes and /dev/uinput; permission errors are reported in the output panel.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The application exits successfully when its eframe window closes normally.  A
nonzero status indicates that native window initialization or another eframe
runtime operation failed.  A failed daemon command, validation, trace, or
service operation is reported in the window and does not by itself terminate
the frontend.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
Canonical installed system configuration path.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
Default per-user configuration and save target when absolute.
.TP
.B $HOME/.config/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
Fallback per-user configuration and save target.
.TP
.B wiilandd.service
Per-user systemd unit controlled by the Overview tab.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wiilandd (1),
.BR wiiland-show (1),
.BR wiiland (7),
.BR systemctl (1)
